## Known quirks to flag in grading

- ChatGPT may **silently use web browsing** even when not asked. Watch for "searched the web" indicators in the response and record.
- Tends to give bullet-list responses; may invert "verbosity without substance" risk vs Claude.
- Citation style varies by model — record what format the tested model produces (numbered, inline link, or none).
- May refuse some financial-pay disclosure questions — flag if it happens (it should NOT happen for public SEC data, but record if it does).
- If web browsing is on, the tool may pull from sources OUTSIDE the uploaded files — disclose this in the comparison table (mark with a 🌐 flag next to the answer).

